### Grading API Tests

Exercises the grading lifecycle with the VS Code REST Client: AI and manual
grades, a revision that keeps the manual grade, a student's petition, close,
and a teacher review after close. See docs/grading-architecture.md.

Select the `local` or `deployed` environment. `baseUrl`, `adminUid` and
`adminPassword` are the variables `toolchain.http` uses; this file also needs
`studentUid` and `studentPassword` for a student account. Set them all in the
Git-ignored `.vscode/settings.json`.

Run the requests in order. They work on a throwaway "[TEST]" assignment made
in step 2, so closing it in step 17 touches no real grades. Logging in again
replaces the JWT cookie, so each "Sign in" switches who the requests run as.

### 1. Sign in as the teacher

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2. Make a throwaway test assignment

# @name testAssignment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assignments/test

### 3. Switch it to link submissions so the student can edit it later

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/assignments/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/details
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{testAssignment.response.body.$.name}}",
  "type": "test",
  "points": 1,
  "dueDate": "{{testAssignment.response.body.$.dueDate}}",
  "assignmentType": "link",
  "description": "Created by api/grading.http"
}

### 4. Sign in as the student

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{studentUid}}",
  "password": "{{studentPassword}}"
}

### 5. Look up the student's id

# @name student
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/person/get

### 6. Submit revision 1; the AI grades it straight away if it can

# @name submission
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/submissions/submit/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "submitterId": {{student.response.body.$.id}},
  "isGroup": false,
  "content": { "type": "link", "url": "https://example.com/grading-http/v1", "notes": "" },
  "comment": "First try"
}

### 7. Petition without a manual grade: expect 409 NO_MANUAL_OVERRIDE

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/submission/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}/petition
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Please look again"
}

### 8. Sign in as the teacher

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 9. Set a manual grade for revision 1: expect MANUAL_GRADE_APPLIED

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/submissions/grade/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}?grade=0.5&feedback=Part%202%20is%20missing&revision=1

### 10. Sign in as the student

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{studentUid}}",
  "password": "{{studentPassword}}"
}

### 11. Resubmit: revision 2 keeps the manual grade (grading.source is MANUAL, grade 0.5)

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/submissions/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=grading

--grading
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="contentType"

link
--grading
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="url"

https://example.com/grading-http/v2
--grading
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="comment"

Added part 2
--grading--

### 12. History: REVISED then MANUAL_OVERRIDE_KEPT_BY_REVISION at revision 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/submissions/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}/grading-history

### 13. Petition the kept grade: expect 201 REVIEW_OPENED

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/submission/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}/petition
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Revision 2 adds part 2"
}

### 14. The student's petitions, without the teacher's evidence

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/submission/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}/petitions

### 15. Sign in as the teacher

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 16. Open reviews on the assignment: the petition from step 13

# @name openReviews
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/assignment/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/open

### 17. Grant it before close: expect MANUAL_GRADE_APPLIED (the gradebook waits for close)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/{{openReviews.response.body.$[0].id}}/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "ADJUST",
  "rationale": "Part 2 is in revision 2",
  "grade": 0.9,
  "feedback": "Regraded revision 2"
}

### 18. A grade for revision 1 is out of date: expect 409 STALE_REVISION

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/submissions/grade/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}?grade=0.1&revision=1

### 19. Close: expect ASSIGNMENT_FINALIZED and grades copied to the gradebook (cannot be undone)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assignments/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/close

### 20. Closing again: expect 409 ASSIGNMENT_CLOSED

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assignments/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/close

### 21. Grading after close: expect 409 ASSIGNMENT_CLOSED

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/submissions/grade/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}?grade=0.2

### 22. Open a teacher review: expect 201 REVIEW_OPENED

# @name review
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/submission/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "REGRADE_REQUEST",
  "evidence": "Checking the final grade"
}

### 23. Add identical submissions to the evidence

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/{{review.response.body.$.review.id}}/similarity

### 24. Decide without a rationale: expect 400 RATIONALE_REQUIRED

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/{{review.response.body.$.review.id}}/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "rationale": ""
}

### 25. Keep the grade: expect REVIEW_NO_CHANGE

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/{{review.response.body.$.review.id}}/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "rationale": "The grade matches the rubric"
}

### 26. Every review of the submission, oldest first

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/grade-reviews/submission/{{submission.response.body.$.id}}

### 27. Clean up the test assignment

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assignments/delete/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}
